# runtime-access.sql is re-rendered into the service directory on every
# `codefly build` — it is the bootstrap image's build context, generated and
# never hand-edited. Keep it out of version control.
/runtime-access.sql

# bootstrap.sql is generated beside it and runs the migration under the
# runtime-access lock before including runtime-access.sql.
/bootstrap.sql

# Postgres credentials. The `local` profile's postgres.secret.env is COMMITTED on
# purpose, as the obin modules' stores commit theirs: its values are throwaway,
# and a workspace composing this module resolves it into a read-only cache it
# cannot write a secret into, so the file travels with the module or the store
# never boots. The repository root ignores every *.secret.env under a
# configurations directory; exactly the local file is let back through here.
# Every other profile keeps its credentials in the provider's secret store.
!/configurations/local/postgres.secret.env
